# L §4.4: "Built-ins on a window (age, add_months, year_of, overlap_days and the rest) give the interval of their
# values at its first and last day. When the two are equal it is that value."  year_of over July 2020 is 2020;
# add_months by one month gives window(2020-08-01, 2020-08-31).  "Only a comparison decides an interval. Wherever
# one value is needed (a print ...), an undecided interval is HOLE-IMPRECISE": days_between(d, 2020-12-31) is
# 153 to 183 days, and printing it is a hole.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

input d: date

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  d = window(2020-07-01, 2020-07-31)

ask q1: year_of(d), add_months(d, 1)
ask q2: days_between(d, 2020-12-31)
=== expect
q1: (2020, window(2020-08-01, 2020-08-31))
  cut 2026-12-31
q2: ?"date within window(2020-07-01, 2020-07-31) not precise enough for a print" (d)
  cut 2026-12-31
